<p class="small" data-receipt-artwork-prep>Receipt continuity · <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/commit/9e4176c">merchant preparation 9e4176c</a> now shares exact-item public artwork fallback between the server thank-you page and the earlier-checkout bridge. All four 390/1440 Light/Dark contexts load native Media Library fixture art, preserve frozen $32/current $14 separation and original storage/new-cart cookie, revoke cross-tab views and exclude images from print. The painted audit is clean; 124 focused units and the full 524-file Astro check pass. Source beta2 and signed 0.8 still omit the canonical number/TEST flag: <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/issues/283">Commerce #283</a> requests that capability, not a release blocker. <a href="/pr-proof/guest-receipt-identity/desktop.png">Desktop</a> / <a href="/pr-proof/guest-receipt-identity/mobile.png">phone fixtures</a> are not original live Orders, signed installation or a complete regression matrix; only reporting is deployed.</p>
<p class="small" data-retained-receipt-prep>Earlier-checkout recovery · <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/commit/d64e2d1">merchant preparation d64e2d1</a>, not an upstream proposal or deployment. The read-only bridge preserves original capability storage and the new cart cookie; four desktop/phone Light/Dark contexts, 111 focused units and the full 522-file Astro check pass. Cross-tab revocation, unresolved-payment refusal and print visibility pass against actual 0.8.0-kernel disposable data and source beta2; the four-view painted audit reports no findings. <a href="/pr-proof/retained-receipt-prep/paid-1440-light.png">Desktop</a> / <a href="/pr-proof/retained-receipt-prep/paid-390-dark.png">phone synthetic proof</a> does not qualify the real ten Orders, hosted Payments, signed installation or complete regression matrix.</p>
<p class="small" data-feed-member-candidate-review>Concrete feed rows · <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/pull/282">Commerce PR #282</a> · <a href="https://github.com/saarius/commerce/tree/fix/variant-feed-rows">fork 07e68fe</a> expands option families into their members, with own identity/money/stock, family grouping and optional host-selected URLs. Same-input compiled main/head proof grows both feeds from five to eleven rows; six native no-script product links match, 885 unit/workflow and 111 integration cases pass in isolated namespaces after the known live sandbox-port collision, and the Registry backend remains byte-identical. All eleven exact-head GitHub checks pass; a standalone re-review was requested after completion. The signed live plugin, five-row XML/CSV exports and all merchant records are unchanged. This is not channel admission, and hosts still need to wire selected URLs for landing-page parity.</p>
<p class="small" data-variant-feed-candidate>Feed control candidate · <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/pull/280">Commerce PR #280</a> · <a href="https://github.com/saarius/commerce/tree/fix/variant-feed-controls">fork 42f0e8a</a> restores one family-level Feeds card for products with options, keeping prices, stock and member identity intact. All 878 unit/workflow and 112 integration cases, typecheck, repository audits and the 131043-byte Registry backend pass; a complete isolated serial run follows the initial runner startup timeout. Four public Before/After captures use actual compiled Registry routes and the native Blocks renderer in a minimal mount, not the full CMS editor. The native hitbox audit still flags small inherited accordion/switch targets; the source has no host CSS patch. Full exact-head CI passes, with review requested after completion; the signed live plugin is unchanged, and XML/CSV option-member serialization is outside this fix.</p>
<p class="small" data-variant-feed-controls>Native feed controls · <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/issues/279">Commerce issue #279</a> records the missing Google/Meta switches on products with Size options, with actual installed desktop/phone captures. Five simple products saved through their panels; two variant families used the documented, preview-fenced Commerce API instead. Agent JSON now exports seven families/eleven members and passes nineteen local Worker checks against real HTTPS reads. Google XML and Meta CSV still emit only the five simple products; <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/commerce/issues/281">serializer issue #281</a> now reproduces the root-price gate on unchanged compiled main, separately from the UI repair; no signed UI repair or external enrollment is claimed.</p>
<p class="small" data-catalog-main-sync>Catalog main sync · <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/dinkuskit/pull/130">exact-size lookup #130</a> · <a href="https://github.com/saarius/dinkuskit/tree/fix/catalog-exact-availability">fork f4f2cbd</a> now merges main83a970f as requested by the maintainer. Fresh bundled-Worker Before/After output retains the unavailable exact-size correction; the diff still contains only four catalog files. All 38 owning stages pass across serial runs on Node24.22.0, including typecheck, Registry build, catalog HTTP, real browser and CMS upgrade gates. Initial agent/auth and shared-store socket failures reproduce on unchanged main, while full candidate retries pass; the externally cut merchant run and its completed retry remain disclosed. Full exact-head Website checks passed at 18:36 UTC, followed by a standalone re-review request at 18:44; review remains pending. The old green retry below is not qualification of this merge. This source repair does not replace the serving signed plugins, and no shared service is deployed.</p>
<details class="dashboard-disclosure"><summary>Catalog #130 · prior-head qualification</summary><p class="small">Separate API proposal: <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/dinkuskit/pull/130">exact-size catalog lookup #130</a> · <a href="https://github.com/saarius/dinkuskit/tree/fix/catalog-exact-availability">fork d0b72c8</a>. The available-only request returned an empty product for a sold-out size; the repair reports that exact input as not found. All 37 owning local verification stages pass across serial runs after an unchanged dev-server retry. The maintainer-triggered <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/dinkuskit/actions/runs/43665891596">complete Website checks retry now passes</a> on unchanged head d0b72c8; review is requested after completion. Earlier attempts stopped at passkey verification and an inventory-runner bind error before cancellation. The successful retry and nine local syscall-traced runner tests do not diagnose that historical socket or make this catalog repair a runner/auth fix; the serial local limits remain disclosed. The actual store feed remains empty under its existing channel-eligibility contract; no shared catalog is deployed.</p></details>
<p class="small">Account continuity is now <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/235">Template PR #235</a> · <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/tree/fix/shopper-session-tabs">fork afe02f4</a>. Generic main reproduces the stale-address write; the isolated shared-client repair passes 74 focused browser cases and the Registry compile, with public desktop/phone Before/After proof. The unrelated local admin welcome/heap failure also reproduces on unchanged main; exact-head desktop, phone, Registry and Playground CI passes, with review pending. Backroad Bum already runs the matching client mitigation, not a new signed plugin.</p>
<p class="small" data-runner-socket-review>Runner reliability · <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/dinkuskit/pull/133">PR #133</a> for <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/dinkuskit/issues/132">issue #132</a>: <a href="https://github.com/saarius/dinkuskit/tree/fix/inventory-runner-sockets">fork 3db2787</a> replaces the inventory test controller’s connect-only port probe with bind/close. Main hangs against a held non-listening socket; the candidate refuses it in 27 ms and leaves its owner alive. All 38 owning stages pass across serial runs, including ten runner tests, typecheck and the Registry guide build; the shared-store socket failure reproduces on unchanged main, then the full candidate retry passes. The earlier merchant failure does not repeat; its cause remains unknown. No single clean local verify run is claimed; full exact-head GitHub CI passed at 07:33 UTC, with review pending after a fresh request. This is a source-only test helper, not deployed commerce code; the exact historical CI collision and the later bind race remain unresolved.</p>
<p class="small" data-checkout-prefill-review>Checkout defaults · <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/issues/236">Template issue #236</a> records an old profile response filling blank shipping fields after another tab changes the shopper session. Merchant <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/commit/bd68be4">bd68be4</a> rechecks the requesting capability after body decoding, with twelve helper tests and twenty intercepted desktop/phone Light/Dark passes. Typed fields, focus and newer sign-ins stay intact; already entered guest drafts are not cleared, and no account, order or payment write is involved. Generic <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/237">PR #237</a> · <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/tree/fix/checkout-prefill-session">fork 5a2980e</a> now has native starter Before/After proof, twenty populated synthetic browser passes, full unit/workflow checks and a clean Registry compile. Exact-head desktop, phone, Registry, Playground and aggregate CI passed at 09:40 UTC; review was requested after completion. The unrelated local first admin welcome timeout remains disclosed, and pending server-cart #229 retains the same prefill boundary to carry forward.</p>
<p class="small" data-profile-feedback-review>Account corrections · <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/issues/238">Template issue #238</a>: incomplete address Save left the missing field unmarked and its error above the viewport. Merchant <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/commit/83ec0a8">83ec0a8</a> adds first-missing-field correction/focus while preserving blank-address, phone-only and Clear behavior. Twenty-two focused units, a scoped seven-file Astro check and 32 intercepted desktop/phone browser passes qualify the merchant presentation, not real authentication or profile changes. Public merchant Before/After images are in the issue. Generic starter <a href="https://github.com/dinkuskit/template-store/pull/239">PR #239</a> now isolates the fix at <a href="https://github.com/saarius/template-store/tree/fix/profile-field-feedback">fix/profile-field-feedback</a> (<code>ab22702</code>), with native main/head desktop/phone proof, 22 targeted browser passes, all 636 units, 118 workflow checks and Registry compilation passing. CI caught a test racing the previous synthetic save response; the follow-up waits for completion before editing the next draft, with eight repeated profile journeys and all quick/Registry gates passing. Full local browser verification stops at the same unchanged-main admin welcome/heap failure; exact-head desktop, phone, Registry, Playground and aggregate CI passed at 12:09 UTC. Review was requested after completion, with the initial test failure and its fix retained in the PR. This is starter source, not a new signed-plugin release.</p>
